WEBVTT

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:20.520
<i>The first time I met her, 
Kukuru's tiny back was shaking.</i>

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.580
<i>What can I say to her?</i>

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.280
Isn't that...

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:54.380
The air pump for the anemone-fish.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:58.390
It was breaking down, so I found 
one that works and replaced it.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:02.220
I guess there's no sense 
buying a new one now, huh?

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.200
Thanks, Umi-yan.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.040
Sure.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.450
<i>There's no more time.</i>

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:15.040
<i>I want a final chance to turn it around.</i>

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.630
Hey, Kukuru...

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:29.810
Fuuka.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.600
What's up?

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.870
Let's go to Kamee on our way home.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.690
Sure, but is there a reason?

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:40.110
We're going to have Udon-chan's mom 
divine a way to attract visitors.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:42.360
Fortune telling?

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.240
You said it yourself.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.800
She's really accurate.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:47.560
I did, but...

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.280
She might have a good idea.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:52.670
Let's do our best, Fuuka!

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:54.920
Yeah.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:56.800
Thanks!

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:58.050
See you later.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:02.590
Ruka-chan?

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:06.490
<i>There's something 
I really want to tell you.</i>

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:12.350
The director who worked on our music video
 before is now working on a movie.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.980
They're asking for you to star in it.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:20.810
<i>They said the part suits you, 
so they really want you.</i>

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:23.780
But I'm already...

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:28.480
<i>Apparently, the agency wouldn't tell them 
how to get in touch with you.</i>

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.120
<i>So they asked me.</i>

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.360
They're an up-and-coming young director!

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.620
I'm certain you'll make an impression!

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:38.820
<i>Senpai, couldn't you please come back?</i>

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.080
Could I get some time?

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:45.050
<i>Yes.</i>

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:50.650
<i>They need to schedule filming, so they
 want a reply by the end of summer break.</i>

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:55.550
Did you do your summer homework?

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:56.830
No.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:58.570
You haven't, either?

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:00.090
Seriously, we're screwed.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:02.400
Summer break is almost over.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:17.320
I finished closing the front entrance.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.000
Thanks.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:23.500
Hey—

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:25.450
I'm done, Kukuru.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:26.760
Okay, let's go.

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:30.010
Oh, Umi-yan, sorry... 
Could you handle the rest?

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:32.390
Sure, good work.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:38.270
Kukuru and Fuuka-chan said 
they're going to Kamee.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.280
They want us to go ahead with dinner.

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:41.820
Really?

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:52.280
Well?

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:55.050
Now's a time of ambivalence.

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:57.480
That's what she said to me, too.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:02.940
Rush into new things, and they'll
all work against you, and you'll fail.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.630
Come on!

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.250
Can't you do something? Please?

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:11.260
I don't know what you want me to do.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.640
What can you do right now?

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:20.680
You might find some new paths if you re-examine 
what you're already used to seeing.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:26.150
Something weird happened, though.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:27.860
That was really nostalgic!

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.410
I saw the dog I used to have.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:31.320
Here.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:34.090
And I saw my dead brother.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:35.900
What did I just see?

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:44.060
Fuuka, you saw it too, didn't you?

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:45.660
The illusion in the aquarium.

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:47.630
Illusion?

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:49.470
What's this? 
What are you talking about?

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:53.600
Strange things show up 
in our aquarium sometimes.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.230
Say what?

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:56.720
Is it haunted or something?

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:58.240
They aren't ghosts.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:06:59.340
Illusions.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.390
It's nothing scary.

00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:03.060
Have you seen it, Kukuru?

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:04.030
Yeah.

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:04.940
Huh?

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:06.200
What's it like?

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.320
Well...

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:12.700
It makes you feel really gentle, I think.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:15.030
It gives you courage.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:16.890
It was like that for me, too.

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:19.230
You've seen it, too, huh?

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:20.000
Yeah.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.960
When I first came to Gama Gama.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.540
Oh, really?

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.750
Sounds like it's a power spot, huh?

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.420
Like it gives you healing.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:31.430
A healing power spot, huh?

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:34.930
It's not just us, either.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:40.500
Some kids who come visit a lot, 
and old ladies have seen things, too.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:41.940
See? Here.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.940
<b>abot_cadd and 40 others have liked this.</b>

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.940
<b>seamore_ayaka</b>

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.940
<b>I had a weird experience when I went 
to Gama Gama Aquarium in Okinawa.</b>

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.940
<b>I saw my late friend.</b>

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.940
<b>I still don't know if it was real or not.</b>

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.940
<b>But it made me really happy.</b>

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.940
<b>#ClownMantisShrimp</b>

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:44.940
It's not just the regulars 
who've seen things.

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:49.320
You might go viral if you share it 
on your official Penstagram!

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:51.080
Penstagram, huh?

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.400
That might work.

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:56.720
I think it'll draw a lot of customers 
if word gets around.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:08:00.160
Karin-chan, do you think you could advertise it 
through the tourism agency?

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:04.490
But I've never seen this... illusion?

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:06.250
Have you, Udon-chan?

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.000
I haven't.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:10.510
How do we see it?

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:16.140
It seems to show up to people 
who are troubled or suffering.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:20.090
Does that mean Karin-chan and I 
have nothing troubling us?

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:22.060
Sure I do.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.040
I get it, Kukuru.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:29.830
But we can't advertise
something so uncertain.

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:31.150
Aw...

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:33.780
Is there anything we can do?

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.600
Onii-chan, it's time to eat.

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:47.830
Look at you, going crazy 
trying to help Kukuru.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:48.920
What?

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:51.130
What do you like about her so much?

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.800
Fuuka-chan's so much cuter.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.380
You should go out with her.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:56.960
What are you even saying?

00:08:56.960 --> 00:09:01.080
Besides, Miyazawa-san is going back 
to Iwate after summer break.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:04.460
I didn't know that.

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:06.150
That sucks.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:14.150
Hey, let's go see the illusion tomorrow.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:16.030
Yeah.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:18.730
We have to try to figure out 
how we can see it.

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:23.500
If we can make sure people can see it, 
I'm sure Karin-chan will help, too.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:25.410
Yeah.

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:28.040
Fuuka, are you listening?

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:30.720
Sorry.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:31.870
What up?

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.100
Is something wrong?

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:35.050
Actually...

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:39.420
One of my juniors called me 
to say there's a director who wants me

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:41.580
to play the lead role in a movie.

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:46.180
I thought you were done with idol work.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:48.180
I was.

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:52.080
But he asked for me specifically, 
even though I wasn't even the center.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:55.160
My junior went out of her way 
to contact me.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.570
So are you going back to being an idol?

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.610
I see.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:09.800
Thanks for the meal.

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:14.090
Kukuru!

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:15.010
I'm going to go take a bath.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:47.450
<b>gamasui_official</b>

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:47.450
<b>Gama Gama Aquarium is the site of many miracles.</b>

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:47.450
<b>Many witnesses :eyes:</b>

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:47.450
<b>If life's got you down, why don't you come 
experience a beautiful miracle?</b>

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:47.450
<b>We'll be holding a "miracle witnessing event"!</b>

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:47.450
<b>Please come visit when you get a chance.</b>

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:47.450
<b>Details coming soon</b>

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:47.450
<b>#GamaGamaAquarium</b>

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.450
<b>#gamasui</b>

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:47.450
<b>#GamaAquariumMiracles</b>

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:47.450
<b>#WitnessMiracles</b>

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:50.960
<b>Abandoned Illusions</b>

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.140
Kai-kun! Morning.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:05.890
Good morning.

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:09.890
<b>konitan_05 Really? What kind of miracles? Details, please</b>

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.890
<b>hasshi-m I want to go!</b>

00:11:08.740 --> 00:11:09.890
"Miracles"?

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:11.740
What is this about?

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:13.900
I told her not to.

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:16.070
This is going to be bad.

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:21.780
Miracles? What?

00:11:22.190 --> 00:11:23.690
I don't know.

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:25.460
Isn't it sketchy?

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:31.150
Fortunately, I guess, 
it's not catching on at all.

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:34.130
Fuuka-chan!

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:35.560
Hello.

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:36.380
Maho-chan.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:37.890
Rui-kun.

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:38.760
Welcome.

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:42.140
It's our memorable first date.

00:11:42.140 --> 00:11:45.660
Hey, Rui-Rui, I told you it isn't a date.

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:50.880
It's just a little outing to reward you 
for trying your best racing against Kuuya.

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:52.350
What's the difference?

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:54.000
It's totally different!

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:57.110
It's not like the two of us 
are in a relationship yet.

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:01.680
I'll do my best, so I can
become a proper boyfriend!

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:02.570
Sure you will.

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:08.440
Hey, are you going back to Iwate 
after summer break, Fuuka-chan?

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:10.890
Are you?

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:12.040
Um...

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.860
I wish you would stay forever.

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:15.610
Right?

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:16.330
Yeah.

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:18.250
It's Kukuru!

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:19.620
Bye, Fuuka-chan!

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:21.670
Excuse us!

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:42.520
We need to experiment, 
so we can make the illusions work for sure.

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:46.360
Who can I ask to help...

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:50.640
Udon-chan.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:52.660
I don't think she's got
 anything troubling her.

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:54.990
Karin-chan.

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:57.420
She doesn't seem too enthusiastic 
about this idea.

00:12:57.830 --> 00:12:59.160
Umi-yan...

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:00.800
He's carrying a bomb on his back.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:02.650
I don't want to make him help.

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:04.650
Kuuya-san...

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:06.900
He's never going to help.

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:20.480
I know!

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.820
I have Kai!

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:30.170
Hello! This is Gama Gama Aquarium.

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:32.370
<i>Hey, I saw your Penstagram.</i>

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:33.660
Sorry?

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:36.510
<i>When are you doing 
your miracle-witnessing event?</i>

00:13:36.510 --> 00:13:37.070
Eh?

00:13:37.070 --> 00:13:40.110
<i>It said you'd explain the details later.</i>

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:41.860
<i>I couldn't want to learn more.</i>

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:53.290
Fuuka.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:55.280
I still have things to do.

00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:56.600
You can go home first.

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:57.770
I'll help.

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.260
Nah, it's okay.

00:13:59.260 --> 00:14:00.520
Sorry.

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:07.450
Okay, Kai.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.030
Please and thank you.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:12.270
How do I see this "illusion"?

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:15.180
Is there, like, a chant that's been
carried down the generations?

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:16.750
There's nothing like that.

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:20.250
I want to start exploring 
how we can see it.

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:21.850
All right.

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:23.500
You've seen it before?

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:24.390
I have.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:25.850
What's it like?

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:30.870
It's hard to explain in words.

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:33.810
I'll do what I can.

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:41.500
I don't think you need 
to pose like that.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:43.820
Oh, really?

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:00.330
So, what kind of illusion 
am I looking for?

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:03.070
That seems to depend on the person.

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:05.680
You see an illusion 
that can help you deal

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:09.040
with something troubling you 
or causing you grief.

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:10.340
Maybe.

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:12.140
Troubles?

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:14.330
Isn't there anything 
on your mind right now, Kai?

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:15.530
Not really.

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:18.600
You're blissful, aren't you?

00:15:19.400 --> 00:15:22.480
Okay, if not now, 
how about in the past? Anything?

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:23.770
In the past?

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:25.450
Oh, what about that time?

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:29.600
When Maho-chan got lost, 
and you cried like hell.

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:31.320
I don't think that counts.

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:33.050
Then... what about

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:34.510
how you were troubled by the fact that

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:36.330
you get seasick, even though
you're the son of a fisher?

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:37.740
When are you even talking about?

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.450
I got over that a long time ago.

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:40.910
Oh...

00:15:59.340 --> 00:16:01.310
Sorry I couldn't be useful.

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:02.360
Nah.

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:05.350
Sorry to keep you behind 
when you have an early morning.

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:06.940
Bye.

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:19.330
Fuuka might be leaving soon.

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:21.760
Yeah.

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:24.520
She did say she's only staying 
for the summer.

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:31.090
I thought maybe if Gama Gama goes on, 
Fuuka might stay here, too.

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:34.890
That was just my own
wishful thinking, of course.

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:39.800
There are new homes for all the sea life.

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:41.600
They're all going to be separated.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:49.860
Kukuru...

00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:53.700
Thanks for the help today, Kai.

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:03.720
<i>Her back was shaking again.</i>

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:11.090
I'm home.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.420
You're home late.

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:14.730
Yeah, I had stuff to do.

00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:17.430
Kukuru, you're going to eat, aren't you?

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:18.620
I'm good.

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:23.370
Kukuru, come have a seat over here for a bit.

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:30.400
I had an inquiry from a guest.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:33.500
She asked when the miracle event is happening.

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:36.150
You put that online?

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:40.000
It'll attract a lot of visitors 
if we advertise an event

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:42.160
where people can see miracles happen.

00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:45.160
I'm sure you know, Kukuru...

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:49.870
Some people have seen it, but only a few.

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:52.420
It's not something everyone's seen.

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:57.680
And no one can explain 
what's going on, can they?

00:17:58.030 --> 00:18:00.400
You don't have to put up an ad like that.

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:03.180
Gama Gama is beautiful enough, isn't it?

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:08.630
But I don't want Gama Gama to go away!

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:21.980
Soon after Kukuru lost her parents 
and moved in with us,

00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:26.240
she'd often cry 
and say she was going home.

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:31.840
She wouldn't listen when we told her 
that this was her new home.

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:39.050
She gradually opened up 
when she started going to Gama Gama.

